# npm configuration for the Nelsen notification bot.
#
# Why this exists:
# `@whiskeysockets/baileys@6.7.12` declares
# `libsignal: "github:WhiskeySockets/libsignal-node"` as a dependency.
# npm v10+ rejects git-protocol fetches by default (`EALLOWGIT`).
#
# The Pterodactyl container image used by this bot sets
# `NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_GIT=none` at the system level — that's the cause of
# `Refusing to fetch "libsignal@git+https://..."` during `npm install`,
# which in turn wipes `node_modules/@whiskeysockets/baileys` and breaks
# the bot with `Cannot find module '@whiskeysockets/baileys'` on start.
#
# Valid values for `allow-git` are `all`, `none`, or `root` (NOT `true`
# — npm rejects `allow-git=true` with "Must be one of: all, none, root").
#
# Two layers of defence here:
#   1. `package.json` "overrides" maps `libsignal` to the npm-registry
#      build (`^6.0.0`), which is the SAME source repo
#      (`WhiskeySockets/libsignal-node`) — just published to npm instead
#      of fetched via git. This is the primary fix and is enough on its
#      own.
#   2. `allow-git=all` in this file is a belt-and-suspenders fallback
#      for any other transitive deps that might still try git. Note
#      that `NPM_CONFIG_*` env vars from Pterodactyl OUTRANK this file,
#      so if Pterodactyl sets `NPM_CONFIG_ALLOW_GIT=none`, this won't
#      help — but layer (1) makes that irrelevant.
#
# Security note: `libsignal` is the WhiskeySockets-maintained Signal
# protocol fork that Baileys uses for E2E crypto. It's a public,
# canonical source — no supply-chain risk.
allow-git=all